{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "L"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 118, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Filling an empty input-to-output edge with a convolution adds a path (experiments 6-10 positive), whereas replacing an existing skip connection removes a useful residual (experiments 1-5 all negative)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "When edge 5 is empty, edge 3 may be the only route to the output, so making it a convolution reconnects the cell (experiment 6: +44.6 on CIFAR-10 versus small changes in 7-10)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a skip from input to output where none exists gives the largest gains (experiments 81, 85) compared with replacing an existing operation on that edge."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Removing edge 3 when edge 5 is also empty leaves at most one path to the output, sometimes none (experiments 21, 23, 28, 29 are the worst drops)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "If node 2 gets no direct input from node 0, upgrading its output edge helps little (experiments 11-12) compared with when edge 1 feeds node 2 (experiments 13-18: +11 to +49 on CIFAR-10)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing average pooling on the last edge with an identity removes harmful smoothing just before the output (experiments 44, 48 strongly positive)."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing a 3x3 convolution on the last edge with a skip removes useful capacity (experiments 43, 47, 49 negative on all datasets)."}, {"edit_edge": 4, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Without a direct input-to-output edge, a convolution on edge 4 provides a key or the only path to the output (experiment 91: +49.5 on CIFAR-10; experiment 92 positive on all datasets)."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a 3x3 convolution on the node1-to-node2 edge for pooling loses learned capacity (experiments 54, 58, 59 among the most negative)."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "direction": "lower", "why": "If edge 3 already holds a strong convolution, turning it into a skip gains less than filling an empty or pooled edge (experiment 87 versus 85/88, experiment 83 versus 81)."}], "tok": 17610, "bad": 0, "probes": [[["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["nor_conv_3x3", "nor_conv_3x3", "skip_connect", "skip_connect", "nor_conv_1x1", "avg_pool_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "none"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "skip_connect"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "nor_conv_1x1"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "nor_conv_3x3"], [3, "nor_conv_3x3"]], [["skip_connect", "avg_pool_3x3", "nor_conv_1x1", "none", "none", "avg_pool_3x